# AutoCAD / BricsCAD commands: collect, specify, classify, and implement

Status: open
Baseline: origin/master
Spec: autolisp-spec/documentation/autolisp-visual-lisp-specification-draft.org

## Summary

Commands are missing from the alref reference, and indeed from
autolisp-spec. As we included system variables in the spec and alref, we
should add the specifications of the commands of BricsCAD and AutoCAD
(and the specific commands of clautolisp — we already virtually have a
few) in a specific chapter of the autolisp-spec.

CAD *commands* (the things typed at the command prompt, or driven by
`(command "NAME" ...)` / `(command-s ...)` / `(vl-cmdf ...)`) are a
namespace *distinct from* both AutoLISP functions and system variables:
they live in the host/engine, are addressed by (localisable) name, take
an option/keyword grammar and a positional input sequence rather than a
Lisp lambda list, and many are package- or version-specific. AutoCAD
ships ~1000+; BricsCAD ships its own overlapping-but-not-identical set.

clautolisp today has NO command specification and only a token engine:

  - Spec: `command` / `command-s` / `vl-cmdf` / `initcommandversion` are
    documented as Function Entries; individual commands appear only as
    prose inside those entries. There is NO command chapter and no
    per-command entry analogous to a Function or System Variable Entry.
  - Implementation: the cador MockHost EXECUTES exactly 10 commands
    against the drawing model — LINE, CIRCLE, TEXT, DONUT, SOLID, ERASE,
    MOVE, COPY, ROTATE, BLOCK/-BLOCK (`clautolisp/cador/source/command-api.lisp`
    `%execute-command-tokens`). Every other command name is recorded on
    the command log but not executed (the interpreter stops at the first
    unknown name). cadtui has no command→tree layer at all (NEW does not
    create a drawing, MENULOAD does not load a ribbon).
  - The only enumerated command *name* list is the cadtui localisation
    dictionary `cadtui/data/locale/fr_FR/command.sexp` (118 names).

This issue covers four phases, mirroring the system-variables pass:
(1) collect commands from the AutoCAD and BricsCAD ONLINE references
into a machine-readable inventory; (2) add a "Commands" chapter to
autolisp-spec built from that inventory; (3) classify them (domain
category + support tier — some commands are package-specialised and out
of near-term scope); (4) implement the categories cador and cadtui need.

## Goals / deliverables

  1. `autolisp-spec/documentation/commands-inventory.sexp` — one record
     per command, per the schema below, sourced from the vendor ONLINE
     references (NOT invented).
  2. A new spec chapter specifying commands (entry template below),
     generated/curated from the inventory. Bump the spec minor version.
  3. A classification: each command tagged with a domain category and a
     support tier (core-now / package-specific / deferred).
  4. clautolisp implementation of the categories cador (execute against
     the drawing) and cadtui (tree effects: NEW→drawing, OPEN→drawing,
     MENULOAD/CUILOAD→bands) actually need, data-driven from the
     inventory where possible.
  5. A generated coverage report (analogue of builtins-coverage.md):
     per-category implemented / specified / total.

Non-goal: implementing the full ~1000-command surface, or matching a
specific CAD build byte-for-byte. Package-specialised commands are
specified-and-classified but not necessarily implemented.

## Phase 1 — Data collection

### Sources (ONLINE vendor references)

  - AutoCAD 2026: the "Commands Reference" (alphabetical) in the Autodesk
    online help. Per-command pages are fetchable as static cloudhelp
    HTML: `https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2026/ENU/AutoCAD-Core/files/GUID-<GUID>.htm`
    (the `?guid=` SPA form returns no content; the `/files/GUID-*.htm`
    form works). Locate each GUID from the master command list / search.
    Harvest across the versions we care about; note version deltas.
  - BricsCAD V25: `https://help.bricsys.com/document/_commandreference--CMD_<name>/V25/EN_US`
    — verbatim description, aliases, and command-line options.
  - Cross-check localised NAMES against the runners' getcname probes
    (already feeding cadtui `command.sexp`), and aliases against acad.pgp
    (already feeding `alias.sexp`).

### Inventory schema (`commands-inventory.sexp`)

One plist per command, sorted by :name:

    (:name "LINE"
     :category :draw            ; :draw :modify :view :file :customization
                               ; :block :query :dimension :3d :render :...
     :aliases ("L" "3DLINE")   ; documented short names (may be ())
     :intl-name "_LINE"        ; the international, _-forced spelling
     :synopsis "Creates a series of straight line segments."
     :options ("Close" "Undo") ; command-line keywords (may be ())
     :arguments "point; point; ...; RETURN"  ; the (command ...) input seq
     :description "..."
     :availability :both        ; :both :autocad-only :bricscad-only :clautolisp
     :autocad-versions "all"
     :bricscad-versions "all"
     :source-autocad  "https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/.../GUID-....htm"
     :source-bricscad "https://help.bricsys.com/document/_commandreference--CMD_line/V25/EN_US")

## Phase 2 — Spec chapter

New chapter `Commands` in the draft org, each command a subsection:

    ** Command Entry: LINE
    *** Name
    *** Aliases
    *** Synopsis
    *** Options
    *** Argument Sequence
    *** Description
    *** Category
    *** Compatibility          ; AutoCAD & BricsCAD availability + versions
    *** clautolisp             ; implementation status: cador / cadtui / not-yet
    *** Source Notes           ; vendor URLs
    #+LATEX: \newpage

Pages are emitted one-per-subsection by `scripts/build-paged-spec.el`;
add "Command" to its entry-type regex for consistent slugging.

## Phase 3 — Classification

Domain categories (initial): draw, modify, view, file, customization,
block, query, dimension, 3d, render, and a catch-all. Support tiers:
  - core-now: implement in cador/cadtui in this initiative.
  - package-specific: AutoCAD-only or BricsCAD-only surface we won't
    support immediately (specified + classified, not implemented).
  - deferred: in scope eventually, not now.

## Phase 4 — Implementation (cador + cadtui)

  - cador: extend `%execute-command-tokens` (or a data-driven dispatch)
    for the core-now draw/modify set beyond the current 10.
  - cadtui: a command→tree layer for file/customization (NEW/OPEN create
    a ui-drawing; MENULOAD/CUILOAD populate bands), and wire spec §5.6
    rule 3 so a bare command name at the `cad>` console dispatches.
  - autolisp-test conformance records for the commands we implement.

## Progress

  - Pilot (2026-09-14): ~25 core commands harvested end-to-end
    (draw/modify/view/file/customization/block) to validate the pipeline
    inventory→pages→build→coverage before scaling to the full surface.
